WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.665
Check that you have the Allen key, four
adjustable round feet, the push latch,

00:00:05.665 --> 00:00:08.380
hinge pin, screws, washer, and cover cap.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.750
Use a hand screwdriver only, and
keep the parts on a soft surface.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:14.932
Steps 1 and 2.

00:00:14.932 --> 00:00:18.111
Lay the metal frame flat
on the protective surface.

00:00:18.111 --> 00:00:21.601
Slide the first side panel
down into the matching slots,

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:24.031
checking the notches match the drawing,

00:00:24.031 --> 00:00:26.960
then fasten it with two
screws from underneath.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.297
Steps 3 and 4.

00:00:29.297 --> 00:00:32.409
Add the second side panel in the same way,

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:37.300
sliding it into the frame slots
with the cutouts facing correctly.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.560
Secure the bottom edge with two more screws.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:42.899
Steps 5 and 6.

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:48.689
Fold the connected frame section over to
form the box shape around the panels.

00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:53.810
Once the edges sit square, fasten
the lower corners with four screws.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.006
Steps 7 to 10.

00:00:56.006 --> 00:00:59.176
Slide the back panel into
the open frame channel,

00:00:59.176 --> 00:01:03.124
then press the four locking tabs
until they click into place.

00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:08.300
Turn the unit as shown and repeat with
the other back panel and four more locks.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:10.615
Steps 11 and 12.

00:01:10.615 --> 00:01:14.783
Place the tabletop face down,
position the assembled frame over it,

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:18.329
and fasten the four corners
with the Allen key and bolts.

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:22.870
Screw the four round feet into the
leg ends, then turn the table upright.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.195
Steps 13 to 15.

00:01:25.195 --> 00:01:28.579
Lay the door panel flat
with its inside facing up.

00:01:28.579 --> 00:01:33.858
Fasten the handle with two screws, add
the small screw and washer at the hinge

00:01:33.858 --> 00:01:37.580
edge, then press the cover
cap into the remaining hole.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:39.357
Step 16.

00:01:39.357 --> 00:01:44.097
This build follows the first door option
shown, with the door opening to the right.

00:01:44.097 --> 00:01:47.866
Insert the hinge pin into the lower
hinge hole on the front frame;

00:01:47.866 --> 00:01:50.950
the opposite-hand door is
assembled as a mirror image.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.410
Steps 17 and 18.

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:58.443
Lower the door onto the hinge pin so
it sits in the bottom hinge hole.

00:01:58.443 --> 00:02:02.900
Slide the push latch upward into
its bracket inside the frame,

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.560
then press until it clicks and holds.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:07.374
Step 19.

00:02:07.374 --> 00:02:11.036
Swing the door closed and
check that the front sits even.

00:02:11.036 --> 00:02:15.662
Adjust the four round feet by turning
them until the table stands level,

00:02:15.662 --> 00:02:19.260
then remember the table is
delicate and not for sitting.
